# Coverage Matrix

> **What this page is.** Every function in the union of (the Cryptol model) and (the production codebase, as reported by the implementation inventory) is listed here exactly once, classified by its proof/coverage status. Functions that are *implemented but unverified* are listed by default — silence is impossible. To drop a helper from this page, add it to `coverage.toml` under `[exclude].functions`; excluded names are reported as a count at the bottom, never silently dropped.

## Coverage summary

| Badge | Meaning | Count |
|-------|---------|-------|
| ❌ | Disproved | 0 |
| ✅ | Proven | 0 |
| 🔲 | Proven (bounded) | 0 |
| 🔒 | Trusted assumption | 2 |
| 🧩 | ABI adapter / stand-in | 1 |
| ⚠️ | Implemented, unverified | 4 |
| 📄 | Spec-only | 14 |
| | **Total** | **21** |

> ⚠️ **4 real functions have no proof and no declared abstraction.** These are the gaps a security review needs to inspect first.

## ⚠️ Implemented, unverified

Real production functions with no proof. This is the gap.

| Function | Source | Maps to | Reason codes | Notes |
|----------|--------|---------|--------------|-------|
| [`canonicalizePayload`](https://github.com/example/protocol/blob/verification/cpp/src/canonical.cpp) | impl (cpp) ([source](https://github.com/example/protocol/blob/verification/cpp/src/canonical.cpp)) | `canonicalize_lp` | `R1 unbounded`, `R2 stl-heap` | — |
| [`handle_provision`](https://github.com/example/protocol/blob/verification/cpp/src/controller.cpp) | impl (cpp) ([source](https://github.com/example/protocol/blob/verification/cpp/src/controller.cpp)) | composes `provisionKey` | `R6 compositional` | — |
| [`provisionKey`](functions/provisionKey.md) | model + impl (SDEP ↔ cpp) ([source](https://github.com/example/protocol/blob/verification/cpp/src/decisions.cpp)) | implementation `provisionKey` ↔ model [`provisionKey`](functions/provisionKey.md) | `R6 compositional` | — |
| [`sha256`](https://github.com/example/protocol/blob/verification/cpp/src/sha256.cpp) | impl (cpp) ([source](https://github.com/example/protocol/blob/verification/cpp/src/sha256.cpp)) | — | `R1 unbounded` | — |

## 🔒 Trusted assumptions

Assumed contracts for real external dependencies. These are explicit trust boundaries, not machine-checked equivalence proofs.

| Function | Source | Maps to | Reason codes | Notes |
|----------|--------|---------|--------------|-------|
| [`hmac_sha256`](functions/hmacSha256.md) | model + impl (SDEP ↔ cpp) ([source](https://github.com/example/protocol/blob/verification/cpp/src/hmac.cpp)) | implementation `hmac_sha256` ↔ model [`hmacSha256`](functions/hmacSha256.md) | `R2 stl-heap` | Trusted HMAC contract; real SHA-256/HMAC code is not proven equivalent here. |
| [`isValidSignature`](functions/isValidSignature.md) | model (SDEP) | external contract ↔ model [`isValidSignature`](functions/isValidSignature.md) | — | Trusted signature-validity contract; production verifier is not proven equivalent here. |

## 🧩 ABI adapter / stand-in

Cryptol definitions with no real-code counterpart (placeholders, uninterpreted functions, ABI adapters). The notes column explains what each one stands in for.

| Function | Source | Maps to | Reason codes | Notes |
|----------|--------|---------|--------------|-------|
| [`canonicalize_lp`](functions/canonLenPrefixed.md) | model + impl (SDEP ↔ cpp) ([source](https://github.com/example/protocol/blob/verification/cpp/src/canonical.cpp)) | implementation `canonicalize_lp` ↔ model [`canonLenPrefixed`](functions/canonLenPrefixed.md) *(bounded model only)* | `R1 unbounded` | Bounded fixed-width encoder used only for length-prefix reasoning. The general string canonicalizer in `cpp/src/canonical.cpp` is unverified. |

